{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733952",
      "title": "Where Should loader() Code Be Stored?",
      "sourceHash": "e1b0c7e1a0348133f29eb7d7bfe88dd0a229687f250cbfd707a9115a9c49a57d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "So we added our loader here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 8.094,
          "en": "You could argue that whilst this did improve our component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.094,
          "end": 12.72,
          "en": "it actually made this app.js file a bit more bloated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.72,
          "end": 15.54,
          "en": "And especially if we would add more loaders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.54,
          "end": 17.248,
          "en": "to more and more routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.248,
          "end": 21.21,
          "en": "this file would start doing a lot of things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.21,
          "end": 23.04,
          "en": "You could also argue that the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.04,
          "end": 25.016,
          "en": "for fetching data for the events page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.016,
          "end": 29.25,
          "en": "belongs to the events page and not to the app.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.25,
          "end": 30.941,
          "en": "So you might want to put that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.941,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "into the events page file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "and not into the app.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 38.25,
          "en": "And for those reasons, common pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.25,
          "end": 41.369,
          "en": "and a recommendation if you wanna call it like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.369,
          "end": 44.46,
          "en": "is that you do actually put that loader code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.46,
          "end": 48.51,
          "en": "here into your component file where you need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.51,
          "end": 49.984,
          "en": "So to the page component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.984,
          "end": 53.343,
          "en": "where you want to add the loader to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.48,
          "end": 57.96,
          "en": "In this case, that's the events.js file in the pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.96,
          "end": 60.776,
          "en": "And here we can simply export a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.776,
          "end": 62.7,
          "en": "which we could name loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.7,
          "end": 64.26,
          "en": "though that name is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 66.87,
          "en": "it does not have to be loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.87,
          "end": 70.95,
          "en": "And you put your code, your loader code into that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.95,
          "end": 73.11,
          "en": "I'll actually turn it into a async function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.11,
          "end": 76.68,
          "en": "because I'm using the async await keywords.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.68,
          "end": 79.833,
          "en": "And with that, that loader code is in that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.15,
          "end": 85.06,
          "en": "Now back in app.js, we can simply import that loader here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.55,
          "end": 90.18,
          "en": "and give it an LES like events loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.18,
          "end": 92.313,
          "en": "Of course, that name is also up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 97.59,
          "en": "And that of course is simply a pointer at that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.59,
          "end": 101.043,
          "en": "which we define and export here in events.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.12,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "Therefore in app.js we can use events loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 106.97999999999999,
          "en": "which is that pointer at that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 110.88300000000001,
          "en": "and use that as a value for this loader property here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 114.96000000000001,
          "en": "And with that app js is leaner again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.96000000000001,
          "end": 118.92,
          "en": "and doesn't contain the actual data fetching logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.92,
          "end": 120.18,
          "en": "And at the same time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.18,
          "end": 123.03,
          "en": "the events page component is also still lean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.03,
          "end": 124.74,
          "en": "because we outsource that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.74,
          "end": 127.17,
          "en": "in a separate function which is now closer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.17,
          "end": 130.41,
          "en": "to the component where it's actually needed though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.41,
          "end": 133.44,
          "en": "And that is arguably the best of both worlds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.44,
          "end": 135.933,
          "en": "and how you should typically structure this.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}